sourceOperatingSections.3. 강의목표:
This course aims to provide students with an understanding of the following topics:
- the principles of electromagnetic forces acting on charged particles under electrostatic and magnetostatic conditions;
- vector calculus and the concepts of vector and scalar fields;
- the electrical properties of conductors and dielectrics;
- the fundamental operating principles of passive circuit elements such as capacitors and inductors;
- the generation of electromagnetic waves by time-varying electromagnetic fields;
- the transmission and reflection of electromagnetic waves at interfaces between different media;
- the fundamentals of transmission-line theory.

sourceOperatingSections.8. 강의진도계획:
The course material will include
 fundamental of electric network theory (i.e., generation and distribution and active and reactive power);
 analysis of poly-phase transmission lines with respect to inductance, capacitance, balanced and unbalanced lines;
 simplification of problems using per-unit and transformation techniques;
 interconnection of electric power apparatus and operation of power systems;
 simplification of power flow calculation and discussion on various optimal power flow calculation methods;
 analysis of transmission line faults (e.g., fault current and voltage) using positive/negative/zero sequence components;

